==Russian==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|sla-pro|ru}} {{m|sla-pro|*uxo}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ru}} {{m|ine-pro|*h₂ous-}}. Cognate with Old Armenian {{term|ունկն||sc=Armn|lang=xcl}}, Gothic {{term|𐌰𐌿𐍃𐍉|tr=auso|sc=Goth|lang=got}}, Ancient Greek {{term|οὖς|tr=oûs|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}}, Latin {{term|auris|lang=la}}, Modern Persian {{term|sc=fa-Arab|گوش|tr=guš|lang=fa}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈuxə/|lang=ru}}
* {{audio|Ru-ухо.ogg|Audio|lang=ru}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun|у́хо|n-in|у́ха|у́ши}}

# [[ear]]

====Declension====
{{ru-decl-noun|у́хо|у́ши|у́ха|уше́й|у́ху|уша́м|у́хо|у́ши|у́хом|уша́ми|об у́хе|об уша́х}}
: ''Note on irregular forms — '''''{{lang|ru|у́ши}}''''' is actually an old nominative [[dual]] form for neuter nouns.

